\f0\b \cf0 Example Usage\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Inputs 
\f1\b0 (see file KICKOUT1.png)
\f0\b :
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 Overhang = 2.75 m\u8232 Distance = 65 cm\u8232 AngleOff = 30\'b0\

\f0\b Output 
\f1\b0 (see file KICKOUT2.png)
\f0\b :
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 KicksOut = 
\f0\b 0.725 m
\f1\b0 \
This means that when the vehicle turns 30\'b0 off its original heading, the outer edge of the overhang will swing out nearly 
\f0\b 0.72 meters
\f1\b0  from its starting path, accounting for the 65 cm of previously cleared space.\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Program Listing (TI-BASIC)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0 \cf0 ClrHome\
Disp "OVERHANG KICKOUT CALC"\
Disp ""\
Output(3,25,"m")\
Input (" Overhang= ",O)\
Disp ""\
Output(5,24,"cm")\
Input (" Distance= ",D)\
Disp ""\
Output(7,25,"\'b0")\
Input (" AngleOff= ",A)\
O*sin(A)-(D/100)
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f2 K\
round(K,4)
\f3 \uc0\u8594 
\f2 K\
Disp ""\
Output(9,25,"m")\
Output(9,2,"KicksOut=")\
Output(9,12,K)\
Pause \
DelVar O\
DelVar D\
DelVar A\
DelVar K\
ClrHome\
Stop\
